findings.body:
**Credentialed CORS now allows any origin.** Returning `Access-Control-Allow-Origin` set to the request `origin` together with `Access-Control-Allow-Credentials: true` means any malicious site can trigger cookie/session-authenticated cross-origin requests and read the responses. The previous `ALLOWED` set blocked that; this removes the only gate.

Restore an explicit allowlist (include any real mobile-webview origins you need), and only attach `Allow-Credentials` when the origin matches. Example:

```suggestion
  const ALLOWED = new Set(["https://app.example.com"]);
  if (origin && ALLOWED.has(origin)) {
    return {
      "Access-Control-Allow-Origin": origin,
      "Access-Control-Allow-Credentials": "true",
      Vary: "Origin",
    };
  }
  return { Vary: "Origin" };
```
